ugh listening and reading  and so i would welcome him to link i'd  be happy to give him advice on how to  you know get the most out of link  and i hope that in the next two years  the canadian election  is going to be in 2019  that he would be able to get his french  level up by that time  uh  just a quick note uh  to end up here  um yeah by the way i am going to  bratislava  and i'm going to spend five days there  at this polyglot gathering then i'm  going to ukraine where for six days i'm  going to do three hours of russian in  the morning and three hours of ukrainian  in the afternoon to try and improve the  level of those languages at a school  which is not something i normally do  we'll see you know how that works out  and i'll probably make some videos while  i'm there now on the conservative party  of canada just for those people who  aren't familiar with canadian politics  uh there's a lot of debate in the u.s  liberals and conservatives and what does  a conservative mean and we're proud  conservatives and all this stuff that  you hear  i would say a good portion probably the  majority of people who vote conservative  in canada  would be moderate democrats in the  united states  certainly  i think  most of them are not interested in  making issues of sort of social  conservatism  like uh  same-sex marriage or pro-life versus  pro-choice they don't want to make these  um  issues they don't want those to be front  and center they aren't part of the party  platform people can hold the views that  they want but  the law is the law and  the conservative party's not going to  challenge those laws  similarly  i don't think there's anyone in the  conservative party who would be opposed  to uh  single-payer universal health care uh  many canadians feel that our system  should be more flexible  we should have more private delivery  uh other more flexibility such as they  have in europe i don't think our medical  system is by any means the best of the  universal uh you